US-012 was already implemented, so this iteration verified it against the acceptance criteria, recorded the results, and changed no engine source.

**What's in place:** `engine/ecs/include/engine/ecs/entity.hpp` and `world.hpp` define the handle as index, generation, and world id. A slot reuse bumps the generation, so a stale handle never resolves. A handle from another world is rejected even when index and generation match. Persistent GUIDs sit beside the entity and do not affect its index or generation. `tests/src/ecs_world_tests.cpp` has 14 cases covering stale-handle reuse, repeated create/destroy, bulk creation, cross-world rejection, and GUID independence.

